\description{
Performs a combined analysis of proportions, treatment-vs-control risk
differences, and tests of risk differences.

The method used for the risk difference and risk difference test is
selected based on the Mantel-Fleiss criterion. If the Mantel-Fleiss (MF)
criterion is satisfied, the Cochran-Mantel-Haenszel (CMH) method with Sato
variance is used for both the risk difference and the corresponding
statistical test.

If the Mantel-Fleiss criterion is not satisfied, an exact method is used.
Specifically, the exact unconditional method is used for estimation of the
risk difference, and Fisher's exact test is used for the hypothesis test.
}
\details{
The analysis function determines which type of result to calculate based
on the current column path specified by \code{colpaths}.
\itemize{
\item \code{"prop"}: calculates and displays the proportion for the current
analysis facet.
\item \code{"diff"}: calculates the treatment-vs-control proportion difference.
\item \code{"pval"}: calculates the treatment-vs-control p-value.
}

For proportion columns, \code{\link[=a_freq_j]{a_freq_j()}} is used. For risk difference and
p-value columns, the control group is identified from \code{.df_row} using
\code{trt_var} and \code{ctrl_group}, and the corresponding \code{\link[=a_proportion_diff_mf]{a_proportion_diff_mf()}}
or \code{\link[=a_test_proportion_diff_mf]{a_test_proportion_diff_mf()}} function is called.

The current column is identified using \code{\link[=in_column]{in_column()}} against each element
of \code{colpaths} list.
If the current column does not correspond to any of the configured \code{prop},
\code{diff}, or \code{pval} paths, an empty \code{\link[rtables:rcell]{rtables::rcell()}}.

The function first determines the current row label from \code{.spl_context}.
If the current split represents the root of the analysis, the label
\code{"Full analysis set"} is used; otherwise, the value of the leaf split is
used.
}
